diff --git a/data/maps/TaichungStationWelcome/README.md b/data/maps/TaichungStationWelcome/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7ea0b93
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/maps/TaichungStationWelcome/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# Isolated Station welcome hall
+
+This is a compact fictional visitor hall for the short indoor welcome and native
+four-starter selection. It reuses `Building` + `GenericBuilding1` source art and
+introduces no custom graphics, palette bank or gameplay logic.
+
+The anchor handoff is `docs/station-welcome-map-contract.json`:
+
+- Registered append-only map group 43, number 13: `MAP_TAICHUNG_STATION_WELCOME`.
+- Matching layout: `LAYOUT_TAICHUNG_STATION_WELCOME`, 13×10 tiles.
+- Player spawn `(6,6)`, elevation 3, facing north; front `(6,5)` stays clear.
+- Optional attendant reservation `(6,3)` faces south behind the counter. No
+  object is spawned and no interaction script is invented without the final
+  Gameplay/Story binding.
+- After confirmed starter assignment, Main directly transitions to
+  `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY` at `(30,66)`, elevation 3, facing south.
+
+The room deliberately contains no physical warp. Its south boundary is blocked.
+The existing Station Gym exterior warp 0 remains at `(32,64)`; using that as a
+physical exit destination would produce a different arrival near `(32,65)`.
+It does not replace the accepted direct handoff anchor.
+
+The first scaffold contains only the map-script label and `.byte 0`, with empty
+events. Once Main installs the guide, frame hooks or dialogue, regeneration
+preserves the existing `map.json` and `scripts.inc` byte for byte. It only creates
+those scaffolding files if missing. Gameplay owns the graphical selector,
+party/state and one-time grant; Main owns new-game and direct-warp integration;
+Story owns dialogue and guide identity. Existing saves are never relocated by
+this source room itself.
+
+The standalone layout registry fragment is
+`data/layouts/TaichungStationWelcome/layout.json`. Root registers it and the map
+serially through the existing pipeline. This builder does not edit global map
+groups, layout registries, C or headers.
+
+Reproduce with Python and Pillow:
+
+```sh
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/rooms/build_welcome.py \
+  --artifact-dir /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/opening
+```
+
+`source-validation.json` checks actual source attributes and graphics for used
+metatiles, grid/border byte counts, elevation-3 ordinary floor BFS, the clear
+welcome lane and anchors, sealed boundaries, existing actor access and the
+append-only map slot. It also checks the existing outdoor handoff cell and
+Station Gym warp without changing them. All 66 ordinary floor cells are connected;
+the estimated map buffer is 672 cells against the 10,240-cell limit. A guide at
+the reserved `(6,3)` leaves65 reachable floor cells. The preservation regression
+check is `python3 -B tools/taichung/rooms/check_welcome_bindings.py`; it verifies
+two regenerations retain a guide, background event and frame-script bytes, and
+rejects a spawn-blocking actor before geometry can be overwritten.
+
+The clean `station-welcome-source.png` and annotated source preview are under the
+isolated `opening/` artifacts. They render native source tiles without a fake
+player/NPC screenshot. Registration and native build passed. Opening-state behavior, selector
+cancellation/confirmation, Chinese rendering and indoor-to-outdoor transitions
+remain integration/runtime checks. `nativeRuntimeTested` stays false here.
