+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: one photo-referenced landmark building sprite study for a north-up GBA Pokemon FireRed-style city overworld.
+
+Primary request: create ONE recognizable Miyahara / 宮原眼科 building in Taichung as a south-facing standalone pixel-art cutout. Architecture must follow Image1, the official owner's real exterior photograph. Images2 and3 are accepted native Station and Theater game art: use them ONLY for pixel rendering, palette restraint, north-up frontal RPG projection and roof-depth treatment. Never copy their building geometry, clock, symmetry, theater curves or entrance details.
+
+Subject and identity: a preserved two-story red-brick corner building with a long rhythmic arcade of dark arched ground-floor openings, tall narrow rectangular dark upper-story windows, pale stone cornice/trim and the pale stone portal around its chamfered corner entrance. Above the historic brick is the distinctive large modern charcoal/slate-blue faceted glass upper enclosure: sloping glass sides with sparse thin light diagonal diamond cross-bracing and a flat rear roof plane visible from above. This modern glass crown is essential to Miyahara's identity. Preserve the photo's longer brick wing on the left and shorter return on the right, compressed for a game sprite. Keep the entry readable near the horizontal center of the lowest facade row. Simplify the real details into clear small pixel clusters; do not invent a station, generic gym, castle or symmetrical courthouse.
+
+Projection and framing: orthographic north-up RPG overworld, seen from the south with modest visible roof depth. Keep the overall front facade baseline horizontal, vertical walls vertical and frontage wide. Reinterpret the real street-corner mass with a shallow chamfered entrance bay; do not copy the photograph's diagonal camera angle, no rotated45-degree isometric building or diamond-shaped footprint. One complete building, centered, no clipping, no adjacent buildings. Target logical sprite160x128 pixels =10x8 metatiles, enlarged by an integer8 factor onto a1280x1024 canvas if possible, using one consistent square pixel grid. The entrance opening should occupy logical metatile columns4-5 at the bottom row; column5 is the future active entry. This is a visual study, not an annotated diagram.
+
+Style: crisp, deliberately limited GBA-era pixel art matching the two native style references, flat pixel clusters and strong readable silhouette, approximately15 opaque palette shades total. Use warm terracotta/red-brown brick, a few pale cream stone tones, deep charcoal/slate-blue glazing, muted cool glass highlights. Suggest brick and diamond framing with economical regular pixels. No gradients, glow, soft shadow, antialiasing, painterly texture, smooth 3D rendering or photographic lighting. Neutral daytime materials, no nighttime bloom.
+
+Background and constraints: TRUE transparent alpha background everywhere outside the single building. No ground tile, pavement, road, shadows cast onto a floor, grass, trees, people, scooters, cars, signs, text, logos, numbers, labels, interface, pokeball or watermark. Omit rooftop lettering and commercial branding. Keep only photographed structural features; no clocks, steeples, flags, red tiled roof, invented floors or extra towers.
