@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: one original architectural pixel-art landmark cutout for a FireRed-style Taichung overworld; first identity study, awaiting native encoding.
+
+Input image1 is the official 2023 restored elevation of TAICHUNG PARK LAKE HEART TWIN PAVILIONS. It is the primary architecture, proportion, material and roof-color reference. Preserve this particular building, not a generic temple. Input image2 shows the actual red timber Zhongshan access bridge: use only its simple straight vertical balusters and spindle-like post heads if showing a very short access deck; do not copy the surrounding lake, trees or people. The pale masonry arched bridge visible in some pavilion photos is a different bridge and must NOT be added. Input image3 is the approved Old Taichung Station study: use ONLY its stepped pixel clusters, economical outlines and game-art finish. Do not copy its architecture, clock, brick, roof shape or soft halo. Input image4 is a native FireRed screenshot: use ONLY the ordinary north-up overworld camera and readable facade/roof depth, not its museum, ground or surrounding objects.
+
+Draw the recognizable Taichung Park Lake Heart Pavilion complex: TWO adjacent square pavilion masses, each with one very sharply pointed four-sided concave metal roof and slender finial. The roof surfaces sweep outward into broad low eaves, with one small eyebrow-shaped louver vent on each front-facing roof. The two roof peaks are separate and of comparable architectural scale. They are joined by a much lower rectangular timber-and-glass connecting hall, whose low roof forms a shallow curved saddle between them. Preserve the pair-of-peaks silhouette, the wide low composition, and the absence of a tall central tower. The real plan uses rotated square pavilion units; simplify their depth for the game camera while keeping the overall front horizontal, without rotating the entire asset isometrically.
+
+Use the restored photo's aged gray-green/gray metal roofs with muted bronze seam accents, ivory-white splayed buttress-like columns that widen toward their bases, warm medium-brown timber walls and window mullions, small geometric diamond window patterns, and a slim dark olive/charcoal curved metal front railing. Keep a low pale platform visible beneath the pavilion. The central hall should have a readable dark ground-level entry in the lower middle. A very short red-brown timber access-deck stub may meet that entry at the bottom center, with simple straight balusters; this is an authored game approach, not a claim about the photographed bridge's exact geographic alignment. Keep the deck subordinate so the architecture fills the asset. No long bridge or lake scene.
+
+The facade faces south and is centered. Camera: ordinary north-up GBA RPG overworld view, slightly elevated orthographic, showing the front and a small amount of roof/top depth. Straight horizontal ground baseline, vertical supports, no photographic vanishing points and no diagonal isometric rotation. The full pair of roofs, both finials, all supports and the low connector must be uncropped. Keep one clear lower-center future entry/approach; no actual game UI or marker.
+
+Target a192x128 logical-pixel sprite:12x8 metatiles of16 pixels. Request a1536x1024 image representing exactly8x integer enlargement, with every logical pixel an8x8 hard-edged square if possible. Use restrained dark outlines, opaque flat pixel clusters, two- or three-tone upper-left daylight shading, roughly24 opaque colors, and deliberate stepped curves. Simplify tiny louvers and railing ornaments for game readability. Match the approved Station/Theater art family while preserving this pavilion's own silhouette and materials.
+
+Return ONLY the pavilion architecture and its tiny subordinate access-deck stub on a genuinely transparent background. All pixels outside that silhouette must have alpha0; visible material should be fully opaque with hard alpha edges. No glow, halo, reflection, detached shadow, fog, gradient, antialiasing, blur or painterly texture. No water, lake, island, shore, ground, paving, trees, flowers, benches, boats, people, vehicles, skyline, signs, text, labels, UI, frame, logos or watermark. No generic pagoda, extra tiers, third roof peak, central tower, onion dome, gate, torii, dragon ornament, exaggerated temple-red tiled roofs, ornate horned ridges, or white masonry arched bridge.
